<title>USA: Rite-Aid completes Thrifty tender offer.</title>
<headline>Rite-Aid completes Thrifty tender offer.</headline>
<dateline>CAMP HILL, Pa. 1997-01-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Rite-Aid Corp said that it successfully completed the tender offer for the 12-1/4 percent senior subordinated notes due 2004 of its Thrifty PayLess Inc subsidiary.</p>
<p>The offer expired at midnight January 22, with $190.6 million in principal amount tendered and not withdrawn.</p>
<p>Note holders who validly tendered their notes will receive $1,167.32 plus accrued and unpaid interest on the Notes of $33.35 per $1,000 in Note principal. Note holders who validly consented to the amendments will receive a consent payment of $5.00 per $1,000 in Note principal.</p>
</text>
